ng the ticket with an audit note, which matches the `resolve_ticket` function. Gate 2: The Solandra platform is active and registered. Gate 3: The function solves the exact problem of logging the resolution. Gate 4: The required inputs `ticket_id` and `resolution_note` are explicitly mentioned or inferred from the SOP. Thus, a tool_call is chosen.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"resolve_ticket\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"ticket_id\": \"{{{{entities.ticket_id}}}}\",\n      \"resolution_note\": \"Identity verified (2 of 4 checks). Temporary password issued via CoreID. Force-change-at-next-sign-in enabled. No OTP sent - admin-mediated reset per policy.\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.temporary_password != 'null'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  }\n]\n\n## MANDATORY CoT INSPECTION CHECKS:\nBefore outputting the final verdict, complete these 3 inspection reasoning checks in order:\n\n- **Check 1 (100% Action & Tool Recall & Preservation)**: Verify that EVERY SINGLE automated procedure step described in the raw human text (whether a shell CLI command like `ipconfig`/`chkdsk` OR an API tool action like `unlock_user_account`/`admin_reset_password`) is preserved in the OKF steps. If any automated action or tool call is missing from the OKF steps, you MUST mark `is_faithful = false` and add it to `dropped_commands`.\n  *(HUMAN CONFIRMATION EXEMPTION: Human/verbal/ticket confirmations, user clarifications, and manual admin approval steps are currently PAUSED. DO NOT flag omitted verbal/ticket/user confirmation steps as dropped commands.)*\n  *(GUI SETUP EXEMPTION: GUI setup steps such as \"Open Command Prompt\", \"Press Windows Key\", \"Run as administrator\", \"Open Web Browser\", or opening UI windows are intentionally omitted from executable playbooks. DO NOT flag GUI setup steps or UI window launches a